279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (As Vietnam continues to attract foreign investment, the regulatory framework for FDI companies has become increasingly sophisticated. In 2024, Vietnam witnessed significant foreign direct investment \(FDI\) growth.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (According to vneconomy.vn, the General Statistics Office data states that the realized FDI in Vietnam was estimated at $25.35 billion, an increase of 9.4% compared to 2023, marking the highest disbursement level ever recorded. Among these, the processing and manufacturing industry reached USD 20.62 billion, accounting for 81.4% of the total realized FDI; real estate business activities reached USD 1.84 billion, accounting for 7.2%; and the production and distribution of electricity, gas, hot water, steam, and air conditioning reached USD 1.07 billion, accounting for 4.2% of the total realized FDI.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
281 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This increase reflects strong confidence from international investors in Vietnam's business environment. To sustain and further promote this positive trend, FDI enterprises must strictly comply with reporting requirements as stipulated by Vietnamese law. Completing reports fully and on time not only ensures legal compliance but also enhances a company's reputation and competitiveness in the market.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
